predicted_resolution:
Enable and point the configuration module to the correct udev-backed config file and reinitialize it. Run:
1) set CONFIG_MODULE=udev and ensure ../usr/lib/config or config.json (as used) exists and is readable; 
2) restart the config module (service or process) and check logs for "config module not properly initialized"; 
3) retry connection.

Most likely root cause: missing config file in ../usr/lib/config causing module load failure.

Action:
1) Verify file exists: ls -l ../usr/lib/config and cat ../usr/lib/config; 
2) If missing, restore or create the config file (from gnb.sa... .conf or config.json templates) at ../usr/lib/config; 
3) Restart the softmodem process and confirm dl/gnb module loads.

Most likely root cause: open5gs NRF service not listening/accepting SBI connections (connection refused on port 2152).

Action:
1) On the NRF host, check process and listening ports: sudo ss -ltnp | grep :2152 and systemctl status open5gs-nrf; 
2) If not running, start/enable it: sudo systemctl start open5gs-nrf && sudo systemctl enable open5gs-nrf; 
3) If running but not listening on 2152, inspect open5gs-sd/sbi/NRF config and logs (/var/log/open5gs/nrf.log) and restart service.
